STRINGS(1)                  User Commands               STRINGS(1)

NAME
    strings - print the printable strings of files

SYNOPSIS
    strings [-adfowT] [-n length] [-t radix] [-e encoding] [-s separator]
            [file...]

DESCRIPTION
    strings prints each run of at least four printable characters in the
    files. Without a file it reads the standard input. The output matches
    GNU strings.

OPTIONS
    -a, --all               scan the whole file (default)
    -d, --data              scan only the loaded sections of ELF files
    -f, --print-file-name   print the file before every string
    -n, --bytes=NUMBER      minimum length; -NUMBER is the same
    -t, --radix=RADIX       print the offset in radix o, d or x
    -o                      same as -t o
    -e, --encoding=ENC      s 7 bit, S 8 bit, b and l 16 bit, B and L 32 bit
    -w, --include-all-whitespace
                            count all white space as string characters
    -s, --output-separator=STRING
                            end each string with STRING instead of a newline
    -T, --target=BFDNAME    ignored

SEE ALSO
    nm(1), size(1)
